        "original_id": "3af7debc-5e50-56a5-b672-6f8b8c9e920e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Cascade Locks and Canal, Oregon Portage Railroad\n- Places: Columbia River, Oregon, Washington, Lake Worth Lagoon, Palm Beach County, Florida, Tanner Creek, Bonneville Dam\n\nFacts:\n- The Cascade Locks and Canal was a navigation project on the Columbia River between the U.S. states of Oregon and Washington, and it was completed in 1896.\n- The Oregon Portage Railroad ran from Tanner Creek, near the future site of Bonneville Dam, to the Cascade Locks during the later years when the locks were under construction.\n- Lake Worth Lagoon is a lagoon located in Palm Beach County, Florida.",
